WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.520
Hi I'm Michael Morris I am the Deputy&nbsp;
Electoral Officer for the Invercargill City&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.960
Council and I'm going to give you a quick run&nbsp;
through about the by-election that's coming up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.800
So a by-election happens where&nbsp;
you've got a sitting Councillor

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.800
who resigns during the term of council within&nbsp;
the three years, meaning that there's a vacancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.120
created amongst the council table so&nbsp;
rather than 12 councillors we have 11.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.480
We can't have 11 Councillors because the number&nbsp;
is set during our representation review process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.520
of how many Councillors we have on each council&nbsp;
so for Invercargill City we have 12 plus the Mayor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.560
which means that if we have a vacancy we have&nbsp;
to fill it. So anyone throughout New Zealand can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:42.000
stand and become a candidate all you have to do is&nbsp;
be enrolled to vote somewhere within New Zealand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.960
which given we've just had the general election&nbsp;
means most people should be and then you all you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:54.480
have to do is be nominated by two people who&nbsp;
are residents of the Invercargill City district so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.880
that includes Bluff in case people are wondering.&nbsp;
Voting begins on the 26th of January which is when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:04.640
New Zealand Post starts delivering the postal&nbsp;
ballots. If you don't receive your postal ballot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:10.400
you're free to come in and make a special vote so&nbsp;
just come into the Civic Administration Building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:18.667
or the Bluff Service Centre. The election day is&nbsp;
the 17th of February and polling closes at 12 pm

